      </tr>
    </table>
  <p><p><font color="#000000" size="4"><strong>Table 3: Outline of the Big Bang Reforms</strong></font><p><font color="#000000">Enacted in Fiscal 1997 (ending March 31, 1998)</font><table class="legacy-table">
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000">Brokers allowed to handle unlisted or unregistered stocks.</font></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000">Brokerage houses allowed to offer &quot;wrap accounts,&quot; which function like combined stock investment and bank checking accounts.</font></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000">Investment trust companies allowed to sell their products at banks.</font></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000">Investment allocation rules for pension fund management liberalized.</font></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000">Financial institutions allowed to establish holding companies.</font></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  <p><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Enacted on April 1, 1998</font><table class="legacy-table">
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Stock brokerage commissions liberalized for transactions of &yen;50 million or more.</font></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Specialized foreign exchange bank system abolished, thus allowing companies and individuals to conduct foreign exchange transactions without government authorization.</font></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Prompt Corrective Action guidelines for banking sector introduced.</font></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">New Bank of Japan law takes effect.</font></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  <p><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">To be Enacted in Fiscal 1998</font><table class="legacy-table">
      <tr>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Banks allowed to sell their own mutual funds over-the-counter.</font></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Allow securities firms to expand their asset-management services, to include and derivatives and other new investment instruments.</font></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Requirement for government licensing of securities brokerages to be eliminated.</font></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  <p><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Fiscal 1999</font><table class="legacy-table">
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Stock brokerage commissions fully liberalized.</font></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Banks allowed to issue straight bonds.</font></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Banks, trust banks and securities companies allowed to enter each other&#39;s markets.</font></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  <p><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Fiscal 2000</font><table class="legacy-table">
      <tr>
        <td height="17" valign="top">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">&#149;</font></td>
        <td height="17">
          <p align="left"><font color="#000000" face="Arial" size="2">Insurance companies allowed to enter the banking sector, and banks and securities companies to enter the insurance sector.</font></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  <p><p><font size="4"><b>Table 4: Recent International Tie-Ups</b></font><table bordercolor="#FFFFFF" class="legacy-table">
      <tr>
        <td>
          <p align="left">April 1997 </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Nippon Credit Bank and Bankers Trust New York Corp. </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Securitizing assets in Japan </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <p align="left">June 1997 </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Nippon Life Insurance and Putnam Investments </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Developing financial products </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <p align="left">July 1997 </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Sumitomo Trust &amp; Banking Co. and NatWest Gartmore Investment Management Japan </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Managing pension funds in Europe </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <p align="left">July 1997 </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan and Swiss Bank Corp. </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Alliance on investment banking, asset management and private banking. </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <p align="left">July 1997 </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Nikko Securities and Smith Barney International </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Joint venture for &quot;wrap accounts&quot; </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <p align="left">October 1997 </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Daiwa Securities and Bankers Trust New York Corp. </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Selling investment funds </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <p align="left">December 1997 </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Sumitomo Trust &amp; Banking Co. and Citibank </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Guaranteeing trust deposits </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <p align="left">February 1998 </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">GE Capital Services Inc. and Toho Mutual Life Insurance </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Selling insurance through Toho&#39;s branches </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <p align="left">March 1998 </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Meiji Life Insurance and Dresdner Bank </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Joint venture for asset management services </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <p align="left">March 1998 </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Jardine Fleming Holdings Ltd., Yasada Mutual life and others </td>
        <td>
          <p align="left">Establish securities company specializing in investment trust sales in Japan </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  <p align="left"><font size="3"></font><p align="left">Source: <i>Nihon Keizai Shimbun</i> (Nikkei Newspaper) 

</div>
